      "name": "Takachiho Kagura Night Dance",
      "description": "Takachiho Kagura is an ancient Shinto ritual dance performed nightly at Takachiho Shrine, retelling the myth of Amaterasu hiding in the cave through mesmerizing masked performances. The full 33-dance cycle lasts all night at the annual Yokagura festival, but a condensed 1-hour highlight version is presented year-round to visitors.",
